      blurb: "Three Poems is a poetry collection written by British writer Hannah Sullivan and published by Faber & Faber in 2018. The book has since been re-published by Farrar, Straus and Giroux, an imprint of Macmillan Publishers. This is Sullivan's first book of poetry, and it won the T. S. Eliot Prize (2018) for the best new poetry collection published in Great Britain or Ireland.",
